= Localhost dashboard
On the repo you'll find a folder: `dashboard`.
This folder contain a python script that emulate a SCADA dashboard.
You will use this dasboard all along the lab, the first step is to run it locally on you laptop and analyze the traffic with wireshark.
You must analyze the http and modbus traffic generated by this dashboard. 

#task[Run and analyze dashboard locally][
  Write a small report with basic information as capture / display filter you used and what you found on packet.
  You can illustrate with wireshark screenshots and concise explanation. The dashboard generate http traffic on port #traffic-port-http. In this task we are focus on the content of the payload. 

  #subtask[
    On pycharm, open the `main.py` file in the `dashboard` folder and run it. 
  ]

  #subtask[
    Open Wireshark and select the loopback / localhost interface. Choose the right capture filter.
  ]

  #subtask[
    Select specific display filter to get only the http traffic and show in your report a packet in depth from the header to the json payload
  ]

]


= IIoT Rack and LAN
Since this task we will use the IIoT (Industrial Internet of Things) Rack.
This Rack (@fig:iiot-rack:hardware) contains several device will see later. We are now now focus on the Edge Router on top right.
You will connect your laptop to this router, experiment dhcp and analyze local traffic. To connect on the router you can use the user: #iiot-rack-router-user with the password: #iiot-rack-router-pwd

#figure(
  image("../res/img/iiot-rack-hardware.svg", width: 80%),
